$ Python matplotlib: Backend and Frontend

The code to produce the plots is the *frontend*.

The *backend* produces the plots.

There are two types of backends:
  • User interface (aka interactive) backends like PyQt, PyGObjects PySide, Tkinter, wxPython etc
  • Hardcopy (aka non-interactive) backends to make image files (`.png`, `.svg`, `.pdf`, `.ps`)

The backend can be configured with
  • The `rcParams["backend"]` parameter in the `matplotlibrc` file
  • The `MPLBACKEND` environment variable
  • The function `matplotlib.use()`

